# Target C branch-recovery index

**Audit date:** 2026-09-04  
**Canonical status:** LEVEL I STILL OPEN

This file indexes research material recovered from non-main branches during the 2026-09-04 all-branch consolidation. The recovered files are part of the main corpus for preservation and reuse, but their historical `Cxx` labels do not override later canonical theorem numbering.

Full branch-by-branch disposition: [branch_consolidation_audit_2026-09-04.md](../../reports/branch_consolidation_audit_2026-09-04.md).

## Matching-contraction regression

- [general matching contraction audit](../../reports/target_c_general_matching_contraction_audit_2026-08-31.md)
- [audit script](../../../research/target_c_matching_contraction_audit.py)

The recovered audit records an exact counterexample to the naive cross-cut sign proof while retaining PSD contraction defect in the witness. Use it as a guardrail for the arbitrary-matching route: the remaining target is a Gale-matrix / matrix-Kalmanson / planar-dual certificate.

## Gate C-I alternate and intermediate proofs

- [formal integrability Gate C-I closure](../../reports/target_c_formal_integrability_gate_c1_closure_2026-08-31.md)
- [facial second-order strictification](../../reports/target_c_facial_second_order_strictification_2026-08-31.md)

The formal-integrability report is an alternate exact closure proof using formal series and real-closed-field transfer. The facial report isolates the second-order exposed-face strictification lemma. The current Newton-Hoffman C63 route remains canonical.

## Response PSD transport currency

- [fully visible response PSD transport](../../reports/target_c_fully_visible_response_psd_transport_2026-08-31.md)

The current PSD response-cut theorem retains `M=Lambda-L_H >= 0`. The recovered report additionally gives pairwise and bounded-degree charging inequalities, including the `tr(M)/2` matching budget and diameter-matching total-variation bound.

## Diameter-class rigidity and reciprocal decomposition

- [diameter-contracted contact rigidity](../../reports/target_c_diameter_contraction_rigidity_2026-08-31.md)
- [diameter-class stress](../../reports/target_c_diameter_class_stress_2026-08-31.md)
- [diameter-component reciprocal decomposition](../../reports/target_c_diameter_component_reciprocal_2026-08-31.md)

These are exact C-II structural lemmas: contraction to full-diameter translation classes, positive cross-class self-stress, and a componentwise reciprocal-polygon/Minkowski decomposition.

