These reports contain special-support PSD/inertia statements and geometric normal forms that remain useful even though their Gate C-I proof target is globally superseded by C63.

## Star max-flow reduction

- [arbitrary-cut star transport and max-flow saturation](../../reports/target_c_star_leaf_maxflow_2026-08-31.md)

This gives an arbitrary star-separating contact-cut lower bound and a max-flow/min-cut stress-transport formulation absent from the later mainline text.

## Two-terminal harmonic corridor

- [two-terminal harmonic corridors](../../reports/target_c_two_terminal_corridor_2026-08-31.md)

This preserves the unloaded-domain convex-hull principle and the exact two-terminal harmonic collapse. Later bridge theorems strengthen the canonical route but do not state this general harmonic formulation.

## Use rule

When a recovered report conflicts with a later mainline theorem, use the later mainline theorem. Recovered reports are retained for unique lemmas, alternate proofs, counterexamples, computations, and proof-route provenance; they do not roll back corrections or supersessions documented in the consolidation audit.
